+### F-309 - Filled contours could not draw clean interior iso-lines
+
+- Status: resolved
+- Severity: medium
+- Owner: API/Documentation
+- Observed in: Solenoid's Recharts-to-TanStack migration
+  (`src/graph/components/charts/fieldFigures.tsx`)
+- Friction: the contour figure needs fine filled bands plus stroked iso-lines
+  at a few chosen levels. A stroked `contour` outlines each filled ring, so the
+  line also traces the grid border and the edges of missing cells. The
+  application wrote its own marching-squares pass over the source grid and a
+  raw `createMark` that serialized SVG path strings per level.
+- Decision: add `contourLines` beside `contour` in the optional
+  `@tanstack/charts/spatial/contour` subpath. It shares grid validation,
+  thresholds, lineage, and level identity, and takes `contour` options without
+  `fill` and `fillOpacity`. Rings come from `d3-contour` unsmoothed so each edge
+  maps to one marching-squares cell; an edge is dropped when both ends lie on
+  the grid border or its cell has a missing sample. Kept vertices are smoothed
+  with `d3-contour`'s linear rule, so lines match the fill's crossings. Each
+  run of kept edges becomes a `polyline` scene node, and unbroken rings stay
+  closed. A sibling mark keeps the filled mark's area contract and bundle
+  unchanged.
+- Verification: internal tests cover a level touching the border (open line
+  ending on it), an interior ring that stays closed and equals the smoothed
+  fill ring, and a field with a missing sample whose lines avoid it and reuse
+  fill vertices. Mark tests cover the mark-name validation message, derived
+  stroke per level, `fill: 'none'`, polylines inside the plot, and projection
+  of the border-touching level.
